
Proposed Amaint options...

I'm not sure exactly what amaint does/doesn't do.  But it sure
would be handy if we could control it fully...

There have been a few users that are forced to wait an hour for amaint
to complete as it does it 'maintenance' to giant CD-ROMs, which aren't
(can't be) any different than they were yesterday.

There have been many users that have accidently set their system
clock ahead a few years.  Amaint is run and it has deleted 1000s
(sometimes EVERY, single one) of user accounts, pfiles/doors, news
files, uploads, etc.  (It wiped out ALL the files, posts, responses to
one of Ken's subboards recently.)

These options could even help to locate any bugs within amaint.  We
could selectively use/skip certain maint-tasks and see exactly which
one is causing the problem.  And we could even avoid using that option
until amaint can be fixed and re-released.

Here are a few 'proposed amaint options'...

-n Purge expired news items (online data only).
-N Purge expired news items (actual files only).  (Use -n -N to do both.)

-g Purge expired gfiles (online data only).
-G Purge expired gfiles (actual files only).  (Use -g -G to do both.)

-p Purge expired pfiles (online data only).
-P Purge expired pfiles (actual files only).  (use -p -P to do both.)

-b Purge 'inactive' items in msg base (online data only).
-B Purge 'inactive' items in msg base (actual files only. (Use -b -B to do both.)

-u Purge 'inactive' items in udbase (online data only).
-U Purge 'inactive' items in udbase (actual files only). (Use -u -U to do both.)

-k Purge 'killed' items msg base.
-K Purge 'killed' items in udbase.

-d Delete 'inactive' users.
-D Delete users with charges <MINBAL.

-r Purge responses in msg bases.
-R Purge responses in udbases.

-a Adopt orphans in msg bases.
-A Adopt orphans in udbases.

+a Delete orphans in msg bases.
+A Delete orphans in udbases.

+d Delete offline files in msg bases.
+D Delete offline files in file bases.

-t Skip all 'testing'.
-T Skip all 'transposing'.

-l No log output (By default goes to "sysData:log/amaint.log".)

-x Don't purge msgs that have been carbon-copied and not read yet.

-f Fake.  Just report, don't actually do the specified maintenance.

-o Adopt orphans with current date/time.
-O Adopt orphans with file's datestamp date/time.

-h This option-list help-screen.

-i Interactive mode.  Do NOT use this option if running amaint via
auto-scheduled events handler.  User this option to pause and prompt
user "Yes/No/Abort" for each destructive action it is about to take.
(ie. Delete a user acct/n-p-gfile/file/message/etc.)

If no options are specified, then amaint would "do all".

Amaint:  *WE* need to control *IT*.
Instead of *IT* controlling *US*, as it does now.

You could also break your amaint up:
 On MON schedule "amaint -n -g" only.
 On TUE schedule "amaint -r -p" only.
 On WED schedule "amaint +d" only.
 On THU schedule "amaint -R -A" only.

Currently 0 of the above are possible.   Even 1-5 options would help.

(Ken, I'll write the option-parsing routines if you decide
to impliment any/all of the above.  No charge.)

